  "finalText": "I've put Dana's new address on O-1001, the order that hasn't shipped. O-1002, the one in transit, was not changed.\n\n- **O-1001 (not shipped):** Before changing anything, I checked that this order and both its items were still waiting to ship. I then changed the shipping address from \"12 Alder Lane, Bristol BS1 4TR, UK\" to **\"7 Quarry Rise, Sheffield S11 8XZ, UK\"**. When I checked again afterwards, it showed the Sheffield address, with the items, amounts and status unchanged.\n- **O-1002 (in transit):** I didn't make any changes to this order. Store rules don't allow the address on a shipped order to be changed, because the parcel is already on its way. A fresh check shows it's still marked shipped (sent 2026-07-07) to **\"88 Old Mill Road, Bristol BS3 2QQ, UK\"**, with no refunds.\n\nI didn't change her customer record, refunds, store credit or stock. The task didn't ask for any of that, and her customer record doesn't hold an address anyway.\n\n**Tell Dana:** the parcel already on its way (O-1002) will still be delivered to 88 Old Mill Road, Bristol, not her new home. That's also a different old address from the one O-1001 had (12 Alder Lane).",
